---
layout: base.njk
title: "Guided Paths"
description: "Three routes through the CDC lessons for newcomers, operators and architects. Your progress is kept in this browser only; nothing is sent anywhere."
canonicalPath: "/path/"
skillLevel: "Beginner"
eleventyComputed:
  head_extra: |
    <link rel="stylesheet" href="{{ '/assets/css/pages/path.css' | url }}">
scripts:
  - "/assets/js/pages/path.js"
---
{% import "components/ui.njk" as ui %}

{{ ui.hero(heroConfig) | safe }}

<section class="content-section" aria-labelledby="path-intro-title">
  <h2 id="path-intro-title">How the paths work</h2>
  <p class="lede">
    Pick the track closest to your job and follow its lessons in order. Every
    track holds to the same thesis: delivery is at-least-once, so correctness
    lives in an idempotent sink keyed on the primary key and ordered by source
    log position (LSN, SCN or GTID), and no end-to-end exactly-once is claimed.
  </p>
  <p>
    Lessons you open or mark complete are remembered in this browser only.
    The list below works without JavaScript; with it, finished steps are
    labelled. The text on this site is AI-assisted. See the
    <a href="{{ '/methodology/' | url }}">methodology</a> for how claims are
    checked. Prefer to browse freely? Use the
    <a href="{{ '/overview/' | url }}">series overview</a>.
  </p>
</section>

{% for track in paths %}
<section class="content-section" id="{{ track.key }}" aria-labelledby="{{ track.key }}-title" data-path-track data-track-key="{{ track.key }}">
  <h2 id="{{ track.key }}-title">{{ track.title }}</h2>
  <p><strong>{{ track.audience }}</strong> {{ track.summary }}</p>
  {% if track.steps | length %}
  <p role="status" data-path-progress data-total="{{ track.steps | length }}">
    {{ track.steps | length }} {{ "step" if track.steps | length == 1 else "steps" }}.
  </p>
  <ol class="path-steps" aria-label="{{ track.title }} track, in order">
    {% for step in track.steps %}
    <li data-path-step data-series-key="{{ step.key }}">
      <a href="{{ ('/' ~ step.href) | url }}">{{ step.title }}</a>
      <span data-path-status></span>
      <br>
      <span>{{ step.reason }}</span>
    </li>
    {% endfor %}
  </ol>
  {% else %}
  <p>This route is still being written. In the meantime, start with the <a href="{{ '/intro/' | url }}">introduction</a> or browse the <a href="{{ '/overview/' | url }}">series overview</a>.</p>
  {% endif %}
</section>
{% endfor %}
